Package: livecaption
Title: Extract Windows Live Captions Text into R
Version: 0.1.3
Authors@R: 
    person(
        given = "Seyed Mahmood",
        family = "Taghavi Shahri",
        email = "mahmood.taghavi@gmail.com",
        role = c("aut", "cre")
    )
Description: Extracts text produced by Windows Live Captions and brings it into
    R for further processing, analysis, transformation, and export. Provides a
    small Windows-only interface for starting, stopping, hiding, showing, and
    inspecting Live Captions; captures manually requested bookmarks with ISO
    8601 timestamps; and retrieves normalized, overlap-aware text between
    numbered bookmarks. This early release intentionally excludes continuous
    capture, recording, subtitle, and Shiny functionality.
License: GPL (>= 3)
URL: https://github.com/Mahmood-Taghavi/livecaption
BugReports: https://github.com/Mahmood-Taghavi/livecaption/issues
Encoding: UTF-8
Depends: R (>= 4.2.0)
Imports:
    jsonlite,
    processx
Suggests:
    testthat (>= 3.0.0)
Config/testthat/edition: 3
SystemRequirements: Windows 11; Windows PowerShell 5.1 or later
